.TH ALETHEIA_CLI 1 "2026-11-04" "Aletheia 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
aletheia_cli \- remove image backgrounds in batch
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aletheia_cli
.RB [ \-o
.IR output_directory ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR model.onnx ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR format ]
.I input_directory
.RI [ output_directory ]
.RI [ model.onnx ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aletheia_cli
loads an ONNX background-removal model and processes every supported
image in
.IR input_directory .
Results are written with the suffix
.B _rembg
and never overwrite existing files.
.PP
The model is loaded once and reused for the whole batch. Processing is
done locally; no image data leaves the machine.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I input_directory
Directory containing the images to process.
.TP
.I output_directory
Directory for the results. Defaults to
.B _rembg_output
in the current directory.
.TP
.I model.onnx
Path to an ONNX model. If omitted, the program searches for
.B u2netp.onnx
next to the executable, in the installation directory, in the models
directory and in the current directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.BI \-o ", " \-\-output " " directory
Write the results to
.IR directory .
Equivalent to the second positional argument.
.TP
.BI \-m ", " \-\-model " " model.onnx
Use
.IR model.onnx
instead of the default model. Equivalent to the third positional
argument.
.TP
.BI \-f ", " \-\-format " " format
Set output format (png, jpg, webp). Defaults to png.
.SH EXAMPLES
Process a folder with the default model:
.PP
.nf
.RS
aletheia_cli ~/Pictures/input ~/Pictures/output
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use long options:
.PP
.nf
.RS
aletheia_cli ~/Pictures/input --output ~/Pictures/output --model u2net.onnx --format webp
.RE
.fi
.PP
Use a specific model:
.PP
.nf
.RS
aletheia_cli ~/Pictures/input ~/Pictures/output u2net.onnx
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 when every image was processed successfully. Returns 1 when
the input/output directory is invalid, the model cannot be loaded, or at
least one image fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project page: https://github.com/MarielCarlosFrias/aletheia
